url: "https://the-sea-going-railroad.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A documentary apparatus for the Florida East Coast Railway's extension
  across the Florida Keys to Key West, 1904–1938, asking who carried the risk
  of the work: seven modules with 133 passages, each read against the page
  image of a public-domain printing. The engineering and railway press
  (Scientific American, The Railroad Gazette, The Engineering Record,
  Engineering News, the Railway Age Gazette, 1905–1912); the railway's
  booklet for the opening (1912); the Monthly Weather Review on the
  hurricanes of 1906, 1909, 1910 and 1935; the Associated Press on the storm
  of 1906 and the peonage trial of 1908; the Reports of the Immigration
  Commission (1911); the House hearings Florida Hurricane Disaster (1936),
  with the report to the President that called the catastrophe of 1935 "an
  act of God"; the Interstate Commerce Commission (1936, 1939); and the
  National Park Service (1938). With six comparisons, a timeline, fifteen
  public-domain plates, and a list of what is not carried and why. Companion
  game: An Act of God.
